onefite-c-code

This repository is an extraction of the C and Fortran engine sources from
OneFit-Engine. Original OneFit code is covered by the Artistic License 2.0;
see LICENSE and the upstream project:
https://github.com/fitteia/OneFit-Engine

Third-party and separately licensed material

1. NAG-derived Fortran routines (moved out of this repository)

local/Florence_c.c/.h and local/Florence_f.f (the latter carrying NAG
copyright notices and historical NAG Library release markers, including
F01BCF, F02AXF, F02AYF, P01ABF, and P01ABZ) were removed from this
repository entirely and relocated to a separately-licensed external
extensions bundle (see .gitignore's own /extensions/ entry) - this base
repository no longer contains any NAG-derived source. Anyone building
against the base repository alone has none of that licensing exposure;
the external extensions bundle carries its own license/notice for
whatever it contains.

2. Numerical Recipes routines (replaced)

core/onefit-3.1 and core/onefit-3.1/modelos once used Numerical Recipes
routines (polint, spline/splint, ludcmp/lubksb, gammln/gser/gcf, four1,
qromo/midpnt/gauleg and the nrutil-style allocators). They have been
replaced by independent implementations that keep the historical function
names and one-based calling conventions; this repository contains no
Numerical Recipes code.

3. Minuit

The fitting engine links separately with the Minuit static library. Minuit is
maintained in the sibling repository:
https://github.com/fitteia/OneFit-Engine-minuit
That repository is GPLv2-licensed; see its COPYING file. Minuit is not
relicensed by this repository. Any distribution that links or bundles Minuit
must comply with GPLv2 and provide the corresponding source and notices.

4. epstopdf

core/onefit-3.1/perl/epstopdf is vendored from CTAN and carries its own
revised 3-clause BSD-style license and copyright notices in the file header.
Those terms remain applicable to that file.

5. Generated and local model code

Files under local/ may contain user-contributed model code and references to
external literature or algorithms. Their authorship and licensing should be
checked before redistributing a build that includes those files.

